@startuml sequence_diagram

title Interlayer Communication: Calculation with Memory Storage

actor User
participant CalculatorCLI as CLI
participant CalculatorService as Service
participant InterfaceLayer as Interface
participant CalculationLayer as CalcLayer
participant CalculationEngine as Engine
participant MemoryLayer as MemLayer
participant MemoryStore as MemStore
participant JsonStorage as Storage

User -> CLI: perform_operation(add, 5, 3)
activate CLI

CLI -> Service: calculate(add, 5, 3)
activate Service

Service -> Interface: perform_with_memory(add, 5, 3)
activate Interface

' Calculate phase
Interface -> CalcLayer: perform_calculation(add, 5, 3)
activate CalcLayer

CalcLayer -> Engine: calculate(add, 5, 3)
activate Engine
Engine --> Engine: dispatch[add](5, 3)
Engine --> CalcLayer: return 8.0
deactivate Engine

CalcLayer --> Interface: return CalculationResult(add, [5,3], 8.0, 1.2ms)
deactivate CalcLayer

' Store phase
Interface -> MemLayer: store_entry(ResultEntry)
activate MemLayer

MemLayer -> MemStore: store(ResultEntry(add, [5,3], 8.0))
activate MemStore

MemStore -> Storage: save(ResultEntry)
activate Storage
Storage --> Storage: write to JSON file
Storage --> MemStore: return
deactivate Storage

MemStore --> MemLayer: return
deactivate MemStore

MemLayer --> Interface: return
deactivate MemLayer

Interface --> Service: return ResultEntry
deactivate Interface

Service --> CLI: return CalculationResult
deactivate Service

CLI -> CLI: display result "5 + 3 = 8"
CLI --> User: show result
deactivate CLI

note right of Engine
  **Calculation Engine Layer**
  - Pure arithmetic only
  - No memory/history awareness
  - Stateless
  - Raises exceptions on invalid ops
end note

note right of MemStore
  **Memory/History Layer**
  - Persists all operations
  - Stores results AND errors
  - Supports filtering/export/import
  - No calculation logic
end note

note right of Interface
  **Interface Layer**
  - Coordinates Cal & Mem layers
  - Handles timing/error capture
  - Provides unified API
end note

@enduml
